## Metal–Organic Frameworks
## Communications
A new method for fabricating CuS nanoparticles in/on a $\mathsf{C u}$ -MOF was developed. The conductivity of the composites is up to $10^{9}$ -fold higher than that of the pristine MOF. They also show excellent activities for the oxygen reduction reaction, affording more positive onset potentials, higher electron transfer numbers, and greater kinetic current densities than the pristine MOF.
